prompt()
  it doesn't work without html file because
  prompt is browser's building function
- Used to read input from the user.
- Returns the input value in String format.


var name = prompt("Enter your name:");
console.log(name);


Number()
- Converts the given value into Number.


var num = Number(prompt("Enter a number:"));
console.log(num);


parseInt()
- Converts the given value into Integer.


var age = parseInt(prompt("Enter your age:"));
console.log(age);


parseFloat()
- Converts the given value into Floating Point Number.


var price = parseFloat(prompt("Enter the price:"));
console.log(price);

